{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94292233734a60f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- compliance\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tPublic-sector deals require the model serving stack to run on FIPS-enabled\n15\tOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules. Today KServe\n16\tcomponents and the serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries in\n17\tseveral images, and we have no compliance evidence package. Certification\n18\tinvolves an external accredited laboratory (historical turnaround: six to nine\n19\tmonths) and mandatory security review board sign-off at defined milestones —\n20\tthese human and third-party gates dominate the schedule regardless of\n21\tengineering speed.\n22\t\n23\t## High-Level Requirements\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n26\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n27\t| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path). |\n28\t| HLR-2 | P0 | A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab. |\n29\t| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. |\n30\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites. |\n31\t\n32\t## Affected Components\n33\t\n34\t- KServe\n35\t- Platform Operator\n36\t\n37\t## Out of Scope\n38\t\n39\t- FIPS posture for workbenches, pipelines, and training (separate strategies)\n40\t- Common Criteria certification\n41\t\n42\t## Open Questions\n43\t\n44\tNone on scope — but note that lab scheduling and review-board cadence are\n45\texternally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"b3e1af7a-9251-4636-a9a1-525220b8111c","timestamp":"2026-10-08T14:57:18.183Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-013-human-process-gates_0_u6qdxlbl/artifacts/strat-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013.md","content":"---\nstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\ntitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance for the model serving stack\nstatus: Refinement Done\npriority: Critical\nlabels:\n- refined\n- compliance\nlinks: []\n---\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nPublic-sector deals require the model serving stack to run on FIPS-enabled\nOpenShift clusters using validated cryptographic modules. Today KServe\ncomponents and the serving data plane link non-validated crypto libraries in\nseveral images, and we have no compliance evidence package. Certification\ninvolves an external accredited laboratory (historical turnaround: six to nine\nmonths) and mandatory security review board sign-off at defined milestones —\nthese human and third-party gates dominate the schedule regardless of\nengineering speed.\n\n## High-Level Requirements\n\n| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | All serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path). |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation states the FIPS support posture and cluster prerequisites. |\n\n## Affected Components\n\n- KServe\n- Platform Operator\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- FIPS posture for workbenches, pipelines, and training (separate strategies)\n- Common Criteria certification\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone on scope — but note that lab scheduling and review-board cadence are\nexternally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94292233734a60f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
