nctionality is not regressed.\n- Build attestations and test results are recorded in a form suitable for the\n  compliance evidence package.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): KServe images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using\n  validated crypto modules, no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n- HLR-2 (P0, partial): produces the build attestations and test results that\n  feed the compliance evidence package.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94006025752471d4","agent_id":"a38a0b360a815ffbc","session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"ebd9ecc7-fd34-43a7-95ea-423f3890c6b4","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:03:09.025Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
