request handling) versus peripheral paths.\n51\t- Produce a gap analysis: per image, what must change to run correctly on\n52\t  FIPS-enabled clusters with validated crypto only in the request path.\n53\t- Flag any non-validated crypto found in serving runtime images outside the\n54\t  strategy's declared affected components — reported as an out-of-scope\n55\t  finding for a scope decision, not remediated here.\n56\t- Deliver the inventory in a format suitable for direct inclusion in the\n57\t  compliance evidence package.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Every image in the declared serving-stack set has a complete crypto module\n62\t  inventory with versions and provenance.\n63\t- Every module is classified validated / non-validated / unknown, with the\n64\t  classification source recorded.\n65\t- Request-path non-validated crypto usage is identified per image.\n66\t- The gap analysis identifies, per image, the concrete remediation scope.\n67\t- Non-validated crypto found outside the declared affected components is\n68\t  reported as an explicit out-of-scope finding.\n69\t- The inventory artifact is reviewable and structured for reuse as evidence.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): establishes what must change for serving-stack images to run on\n74\t  FIPS-enabled clusters with validated crypto — identifies the gaps.\n75\t- HLR-2 (P0): the module inventory is an explicit component of the compliance\n76\t  evidence package.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9719ed011d20632","agent_id":"a51e6c56cfa0c7e4c","session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"571cb72f-65fe-49a7-90be-cde7203414a9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:06:40.570Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a333af8f236f23b2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
