reuse in the compliance\n51\t  evidence package.\n52\t- Coordinate with the image rebuilds so downstream consumers of the images can\n53\t  pick up remediated versions.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- All remediated KServe images contain no non-validated cryptographic modules\n58\t  in the request path, per the module inventory classification.\n59\t- Remediated images run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters.\n60\t- Inference request handling works end to end on a FIPS-enabled cluster in\n61\t  both serverless and raw deployment modes (InferenceService CRs reach Ready\n62\t  with correct predictor status).\n63\t- Existing serving functionality is not regressed.\n64\t- Build attestations and test results are recorded in a form suitable for the\n65\t  compliance evidence package.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): KServe images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using\n70\t  validated crypto modules, no non-validated crypto in the request path.\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0, partial): produces the build attestations and test results that\n72\t  feed the compliance evidence package.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9719ed011d20632","agent_id":"a51e6c56cfa0c7e4c","session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"cf8c276b-cc12-4d60-bb45-123ca635ebb3","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:06:41.241Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b44e6b7e3e86b4bd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
