e package.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The remediated Platform Operator image contains no non-validated\n55\t  cryptographic modules in the request path, per the module inventory\n56\t  classification.\n57\t- The operator installs and reconciles correctly on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift\n58\t  cluster.\n59\t- Existing operator functionality is not regressed.\n60\t- Build attestations and test results are recorded in a form suitable for the\n61\t  compliance evidence package.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-1 (P0): the Platform Operator image runs correctly on FIPS-enabled\n66\t  clusters using validated crypto modules.\n67\t- HLR-2 (P0, partial): produces the operator's build attestations and test\n68\t  results that feed the compliance evidence package.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9719ed011d20632","agent_id":"a51e6c56cfa0c7e4c","session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"12c9b068-20e6-4266-b98e-669f48d4fe89","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:06:41.794Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab9ca650b60202a1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
