{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9edf0669579edbed","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n3\ttitle: CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions on serving-stack builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions on serving-stack builds\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAdd a gating CI check that fails any serving-stack build which reintroduces\n35\tnon-validated cryptographic usage, so FIPS compliance cannot silently regress\n36\tonce remediation lands.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Implement a build-time check (or extend existing build checks) that inspects\n41\t  serving-stack build artifacts/images for non-validated cryptographic module\n42\t  usage, based on the validated/non-validated classification from the module\n43\t  inventory.\n44\t- Wire the check into the serving-stack build pipelines as a gating (blocking)\n45\t  step, so a failing check fails the build.\n46\t- Make the classification data maintainable: when the validated-module list\n47\t  changes, the check's rules can be updated without re-engineering the check.\n48\t- Handle the request-path distinction from the module inventory so the gate\n49\t  enforces the same requirement the remediation delivers (no non-validated\n50\t  crypto in the request path).\n51\t- Document for build maintainers how to interpret and act on a gate failure.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- A serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated cryptographic usage\n56\t  in the request path fails the gating check.\n57\t- A compliant build passes the gating check (no false failures on remediated\n58\t  images).\n59\t- The check is gating — it blocks merge/release of failing builds, not merely\n60\t  advisory.\n61\t- The validated/non-validated classification the check uses is derived from\n62\t  and kept consistent with the module inventory.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1): CI enforces FIPS regressions; a gating check fails any\n67\t  serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9719ed011d20632","agent_id":"a51e6c56cfa0c7e4c","session_id":"d93786ac-0085-40fb-b807-b5feb6113de8","uuid":"f3edac33-2870-4b04-b239-6971a050d1c6","timestamp":"2026-10-08T15:07:00.080Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9edf0669579edbed","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
